; onehotr_spin_model: ONEHOTR on a spin {-1, +1} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; ONEHOTR writes a one-hot penalty over grid row 0, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which holds only for binary
; variables. On any other domain the same terms encode a different penalty,
; so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has ONEHOTR raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
SQMX r0          ; spin model, 4 variables
PUSH 2           ; rows
PUSH 2           ; cols
RESIZE r0        ; 2x2 grid, so the grid precondition holds
PUSH 0           ; row
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
